    "If West discards on the first round of diamonds, East will have 2 certain stoppers. South should win in dummy and play on clubs. If clubs are 3-2, the contract still will make.",
    "It takes a combination of 4-1 clubs and East having all 4 diamonds to defeat this line of play. An equally effective line of play would be to cash the ♣A and ♣K before playing diamonds. If clubs are 3-2, a trick can be surrendered in clubs. If clubs break badly, South can play diamonds as before."
